The formulae we obtain for the structure constants Cλ,μν,dC_{\lambda,\mu}^{
u,d} arise from solving a certain system of linear equations, and are combinatorially explicit (cf. Theorem 6.2 and Theorem 6.3 below), but not cancellation free. Due to their equivariant nature, one may think of them as related to formulae for Schubert structure constants using Chevalley recursions [62, 18]. In fact, our formulae seem new already in the classical ring KT​(X)\,\mathrm{K}_{T}(X), the equivariant K-theory of Grassmannians. The cylindric Grothendieck polynomials in (II) generalize both Postnikov’s toric Schur functions and McNamara’s factorial (skew) Grothendieck polynomials [60], and also Yeliussizov’s modified Grothendieck polynomials [71].
